---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro'
import {SITE} from '../lib/site.js'
---

<PageLayout
  title="About / Our History"
  kicker="About"
  intro={`${SITE.name} is Georgetown University's student-run international affairs newspaper.`}
>
  <!-- TODO: replace placeholder copy with the real history from the Squarespace "Our History" page. -->
  <p>
    The Caravel was founded by students in the School of Foreign Service to cover world affairs from
    a campus that sends more graduates into diplomacy and international work than almost any other.
    Since then it has grown into a fully student-edited publication with regional desks, a Compass
    sub-brand for cross-cutting themes, and an alumni network reporting from around the world.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>
    Six regional desks — Africa; Eastern Europe &amp; Central Asia; Indo-Asia-Pacific; Latin America
    &amp; The Caribbean; Southwest Asia &amp; North Africa; and Western Europe &amp; Canada — plus
    Opinion &amp; Satire, Travel, and long-form features in the Crow's Nest. The Caravel Compass
    follows six themes across every region: World, Elections, Gender, Coin, Futures, and Planet.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    The Caravel is editorially independent and student-owned. It is not an official publication of
    Georgetown University, and the views expressed are those of the authors.
  </p>

  <h2>Get involved</h2>
  <p>
    We take pitches from any Georgetown student — no prior experience or newsroom role required. See
    <a href="/join">Join Our Team</a> for how the submission process works, or
    <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
